      "question": "Do I need a radon test?",
      "answer": "The EPA recommends radon testing for all residential homes located below the third floor. Radon is an invisible, odorless radioactive gas that enters buildings through foundation cracks and soil contact. Because standard inspections do not evaluate radon concentrations, you must request a specialized radon test."
