    {
      "question": "What extra checks does an older house need?",
      "answer": "Older properties require targeted evaluations for obsolete materials and past construction practices. Homes built before 1978 require lead-based paint disclosures, while properties built before 1950 frequently feature knob-and-tube wiring. Inspectors also check for pre-1986 lead solder or pipes, mid-century aluminum wiring, suspect asbestos insulation, and aging sewer lines that require camera inspection."
    },
