      "question": "How do I use the inspection report to negotiate?",
      "answer": "Review the final written report and separate urgent safety issues and major mechanical failures from routine cosmetic flaws. Contact licensed tradespeople to obtain formal written repair estimates for the significant defects. Submit these documented repair costs to the seller to request price reductions or closing credits before your contingency deadline lapses."
